@startuml descriptor-governance
' Sources:
'   src/charter/offering/drg/models.py        (DRGGraph, DRGNode, DRGEdge, NodeKind, Relation)
'   src/charter/activation/schemas.py         (GovernanceCharterConfig)
'   src/charter/offering/packs/pack_descriptor.py (PackDescriptor -> pack.yaml)
'   see also core src/charter/diagrams/pack-descriptor-model.puml
' Decided design: ADR-0048 (composition), ADR-0049 (glossary), ADR-0050 (mission types, lifecycles, gates),
' ADR-0051 (event registry), ADR-0052 (anti-patterns). Accepted 2026-11-02; none of it is built yet.
' Pending: a yellow <<pending>> class or a [pending ADR-00xx OQn] suffix marks a part whose open question is not ruled.
!include _style.iuml
title Pack, DRG and charter configuration schemas — decided design (ADR-0048…ADR-0052)

class PackDescriptor <<pack.yaml>> {
  + pack_id : string [ULID pattern]
  + pack_version : string [every level]
  - parent_pack : string [ULID pattern; lineage only, sets no load order]
  - depends_on : DependsOn[]
  + name : string
  - pack_level : PackTier <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0048 OQ7: required?]</color>
  - requires_core : string
  - pack_drg : path
}
class DependsOn <<item of depends_on>> {
  + pack_id : string [ULID]
  + range : string <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0048 OQ4: grammar]</color>
}
class DRGGraph <<*.graph.yaml>> {
  + schema_version : "1.0"
  + generated_at : string
  - generated_by : string
  + nodes : DRGNode[]
  + edges : DRGEdge[]
}
class DRGNode {
  + urn : string  "<kind>:<id>"
  + kind : NodeKind
  - label : string
  - provenance : string
  - tags : string[] = []
}
class DRGEdge {
  + source : string [URN only; DIV-007]
  + target : string [URN only; DIV-007]
  + relation : Relation
  - when : string
  - reason : string
  - impacts : number [shards only]
}
enum NodeKind {
  directive, tactic, paradigm, styleguide,
  toolguide, procedure, agent_profile,
  mission_step_contract, template, asset,
  action, term, mission_type,
  anti_pattern, skill, lifecycle
  glossary <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0049 OQ3: core node clash]</color>
  gate <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0050 OQ2]</color>
  event_registry <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0051 OQ3]</color>
}
enum Relation {
  requires, suggests, applies, scope,
  vocabulary, instantiates, replaces,
  delegates_to, specializes_from, enhances,
  overrides, refines, in_tension_with,
  reconciles_tension, rejects
}
class GovernanceCharterConfig <<project charter>> {
  - selected_paradigms, selected_directives,
    selected_tactics, selected_styleguides,
    selected_toolguides, selected_procedures,
    selected_agent_profiles,
    selected_mission_step_contracts,
    selected_mission_types, selected_anti_patterns,
    selected_<glossary plural>,
    selected_assets : string[] = []
  - available_tools : string[]
  - template_set : string
  - authority_paths : string[]
  - governance_references : string[]
}
PackDescriptor "1" *-- "0..*" DependsOn
PackDescriptor --> "0..1" DRGGraph : pack_drg
DRGGraph *-- "*" DRGNode
DRGGraph *-- "*" DRGEdge
DRGNode --> NodeKind
DRGEdge --> Relation
DRGEdge ..> DRGNode : source / target
note bottom of NodeKind
  glossary_scope is retired (ADR-0049 d11): scope comes from the pack level.
  Token spelling is snake_case (mission_type, anti_pattern, event_registry) <color:#8A6D00>[pending ADR-0050 OQ9]</color>
  vocabulary targets glossary and term (ADR-0049 d4).
end note
note bottom of PackDescriptor
  org-charter.yaml and active_charter are retired (#431): org enforcement is a governing
  preset (presets/<id>.yaml, must_have items) plus policy.yaml levels (ADR-0063).
end note
note bottom of GovernanceCharterConfig
  <glossary plural> is not spelled by ADR-0049 (follow-up #114).
  selected_mission_types and selected_anti_patterns are derived names, not in any schema yet.
end note
note bottom of DRGGraph
  An org fragment (drg/fragment.yaml) has nodes and edges only, no header fields (DIV-008).
  An edge carries no provenance (DIV-019); a shard node may.
end note
legend right
  Yellow <<pending>> / [pending …]: decided in the cited ADR,
  but the cited open question is not ruled.
endlegend
@enduml
